  "id": "COMPOUND:37601 - PROTEIN:5807",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a direct relationship between the compound [(3S,5aS,6S,7S,9aS)-6-[2-[(5aS,6S,7R,9aS)-7-acetyloxy-2,2,5a,7-tetramethyl-3-oxo-4,5,6,8,9,9a-hexahydrobenzo[b]oxepin-6-yl]ethyl]-7-acetyloxy-2,2,5a,7-tetramethyl-4,5,6,8,9,9a-hexahydro-3H-benzo[b]oxepin-3-yl] acetate and prostate cells, through a series of target interactions. The compound is identified as a target of multiple substances, including 5-(2-Thienylethynyl)-2-thiophenemethanol, (2R,3S,4S,5R,6S)-2-(Hydroxymethyl)-6-[3-[(E)-3-Hydroxyprop-1-Enyl]-2,5-Dimethoxyphenoxy]Oxane-3,4,5-Triol, and Lethedioside B, all of which are known to interact with microtubule-associated protein 1B. This protein is a known target of prostate cells, indicating a potential mechanism by which the compound may exert its effects on prostate cells. The evidence suggests that the compound may act through a pathway involving microtubule-associated protein 1B, which is a key player in cellular processes related to prostate cell function. The integration of these pathways highlights the compound's potential role in modulating prostate cell behavior, though further studies are needed to fully elucidate the mechanism.",
